  "title": "P3/P6 wiring, shadow only: build evidence candidates from the execute and review packet builders, route them, log context_selection decisions and shadow reduction into packet_meta and the context scorecard; the model still receives the unchanged packet",
  "spec": "Depends on T-0794 (orchestrator/evidence.py, orchestrator/context_router.py: make(), EvidencePool, route(), render(), decision_row() which returns the full keyword set for decision_log.record), T-0772 (promotion.mode(\"context_router\"), decision_log kind context_selection) and T-0799 (execute prompt dedup; spawn.py changed there). This spec is self-contained; the program brief is not on the goal branch. Shadow means: compute and log; the bytes sent to any model are byte-identical to before this task (assert in tests).\nDo:\n1. spawn.py, execute path (_packet_body around lines 181-350): after `sections` are assembled and before the cap loop, build candidates via evidence.make(): one \"architecture_note\" for task spec (location task:<id>:spec) and one per acceptance line (task:<id>:acceptance:<n>); one \"source_chunk\" per write-scope file that exists (content = the file text bounded to 12000 chars, commit = merge_base sha) and one per read_scope path (content = the symbols lines for that path, provenance repo); one \"memory_entry\" per gotcha line and one \"decision\" per decisions line (provenance memory); one \"previous_result\" per evidence line from task inputs (provenance bus, trust untrusted); one \"test_result\" for each relevant_tests path (content = path only) and, for fix rounds, one for the failure block in the spec if a \"Failures:\" marker exists (content = that block). Add every candidate to evidence.EvidencePool(goal) (goal = task parent or task id). Call context_router.route(task, candidates, role=\"execute\", head_sha=merge_base, cfg=Pool().cfg). When promotion.mode(\"context_router\") == \"off\": skip everything in this step. When \"shadow\" or \"active\" (active is treated as shadow in this task and logs a warning once per process via notify: \"context_router active not implemented; running shadow\"): record decision_log.record(**context_router.decision_row(task, routed, mode=mode)) and extend the build meta returned by _packet_body with routed_tokens, routed_reduction_ratio, routed_hidden, routed_ambiguous, routed_rules_version, evidence_ids (list of ids, capped 200). packet_run_meta / with_instruction_tokens / bus.log_run (P1) must carry those keys through into the run's `context` object (bus.py: add the keys to the copied list). The router must never raise into the packet builder: wrap in try/except, log one notify line, and continue without the shadow keys.\n2. spawn.py, review path (review_packet ~435-500): candidates = the scoped diff as one \"source_chunk\" per file hunk group (split raw_diff on \"diff --git\", location = the path, content = that file's hunks), spec/acceptance notes as above, previous review comments (fix-round context) as \"review_finding\". role = \"security_review\" when the packet carries the security section, else \"review\". Same logging and meta keys, same shadow guarantee.\n3. context_scorecard.py: per role and per goal add columns shadow_routed_tokens (avg), shadow_reduction (avg routed_reduction_ratio), shadow_hidden (avg), shadow_ambiguous_rate (ambiguous / candidates); rows without the keys count as unmeasured for those columns only. `orchestrator scorecard --context` prints them.\n4. Scout evidence reuse (P8 first step): scout_evidence.reuse_check may read evidence.EvidencePool(goal) ids by source_type \"scout_finding\" only if it is a one-line addition; otherwise leave scout_evidence untouched and note it.\nTests: tests/test_spawn.py::test_execute_packet_bytes_unchanged_under_context_router_shadow (build a packet with mode off and with mode shadow on the same fixture task; the packet text is identical; the shadow meta keys exist only in shadow), ::test_execute_packet_logs_context_selection_decision (one decision_log row of kind context_selection with subject = task id, no content field in the row), ::test_review_packet_routes_diff_files_per_path (a two-file diff gives two source_chunk candidates with those locations), ::test_router_failure_never_breaks_packet (monkeypatch context_router.route to raise; packet still builds; a notify line mentions the task); tests/test_context_scorecard.py::test_shadow_columns_present_and_unmeasured_rows_counted; tests/test_bus.py::test_log_run_carries_routed_keys.\nDocs: extend docs/context-economy/05-context-router.md with a \"Shadow wiring\" section (what is logged where, how to read the scorecard columns, revert path: set [context_router] mode = \"off\" or git revert). Do not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.",
